  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 240 AM EDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nMuch cooler this morning with clear skies and light northerly\nwinds allowing for ideal radiational cooling. Dew points in the\nlow to mid 40s across the area will keep lows close to these\nvalues. Some patchy mist/fog will be possible but should remain\nnear surface and the light winds will help to mix drier air\nkeeping any mist/fog very localized. \n\nHighs today with mostly sunny skies will again be in the mid\n60s. Lows tonight will run a degree or two cooler with slightly\ndrier air in place, however a weak trough moving eastward into\nthe region will allow for increased WAA ahead of the upper level\ntroughing and highs on Sunday will be warmer with highs slightly\nwarmer getting into the lower 70s across the area. In the wake\nof the weak disturbance a northwesterly to zonal flow will\nreturn across the region with synoptic cooling returning, lows\nMonday morning back into the low to mid 40s and highs on Monday\nonly in the low to mid 60s. This pattern also brings a shot of\ndrier airmass into the region and will bring a crisp morning on\nTuesday with lows in the mid to upper 30s, BRRRRRRR. Should make\nfor good sleeping weather, may also want to plan on protecting\nany very temperature sensitive plants/animals out of an\nabundance of caution. Still thinking that some isolated frost \non more elevated surfaces will be possible but with still very \nmoist and warm soils should keep any frost development at bay. \nWill continue to keep an eye on this situation. With a more \nnorthwesterly flow into the later part of the week and slightly \nhigher synoptic heights arriving dry conditions look to continue\nwith slight warming into the end of the week when highs \nWednesday and onward into the 70s.",
